# Typography: "quotes", 'quotes' and don't

"Double quotes" and 'single quotes' open after a blank and close after a word, so don't, (a "bracketed" quote) and a quote after a dash--"like this".
A quote starts a line, so "this one opens" after the soft break.

Dots and dashes: wait... a pause, an em dash--here, then ---, then ...., and a lone - or .. as they are.

_"Emphasis is transparent"_, and *'strong' too*; after a word_"even here"_ a quote closes, as it does in "_this_".

Code is left alone: `'code' "span" -- ...`, and so is the target and the alt: [@a "link" that's text](https://example.com/it's "x") and [!"pic" it's](pic.png).

Code spans, images and notes count as letters: `c`"closes", [!pic](pic.png)"closes", and a note[^n]"closes".

An escape keeps its characters apart: -\- and \-- and \-"opens".

- 'A list item' starts afresh
- and so does "this one"

>
"A quote" starts afresh, too.
<

[^n]: 'A note' starts afresh, and so does "this" one.
